From 85e56c3bbb7e8ea4626f8653afaef0d79d9cb7ba Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bui duc phuc <phucduc.bui@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 17:38:25 +0700
Subject: ASoC: imx-pcm-rpmsg: Fix imx_rpmsg_pcm_close() being skipped on rollback
Git-commit: 85e56c3bbb7e8ea4626f8653afaef0d79d9cb7ba
Patch-mainline: v7.4-rc1
References: git-fixes

snd_pcm_hw_constraint_integer() may return 1, which is then returned
from imx_rpmsg_pcm_open(). ASoC only marks the component as opened
when .open() returns 0, so .close() can be skipped on rollback.

Return 0 explicitly on success.

Fixes: 3c00eceb2a53 ("ASoC: imx-pcm-rpmsg: Add platform driver for audio base on rpmsg")
Signed-off-by: bui duc phuc <phucduc.bui@gmail.com>
Link: https://patch.msgid.link/20261008103831.542533-19-phucduc.bui@gmail.com
Signed-off-by: Mark Brown <broonie@kernel.org>
Acked-by: Takashi Iwai <tiwai@suse.de>

---
 sound/soc/fsl/imx-pcm-rpmsg.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/fsl/imx-pcm-rpmsg.c b/sound/soc/fsl/imx-pcm-rpmsg.c
index 7086fb7fc1eb..30e75fee5175 100644
--- a/sound/soc/fsl/imx-pcm-rpmsg.c
+++ b/sound/soc/fsl/imx-pcm-rpmsg.c
@@ -269,7 +269,7 @@ static int imx_rpmsg_pcm_open(struct snd_soc_component *component,
 	info->stream_timer[substream->stream].substream = substream;
 	timer_setup(&info->stream_timer[substream->stream].timer,
 		    imx_rpmsg_timer_callback, 0);
-	return ret;
+	return 0;
 }
 
 static int imx_rpmsg_pcm_close(struct snd_soc_component *component,
-- 
